---
/**
 * Where a donor lands after completing a gift. This is the URL to enter as
 * the return address on the PayPal gift button:
 *
 *   https://friendsofthelatimerhouse.org/thank-you/gift/
 *
 * In PayPal this is "Take customers to this URL when they finish checkout"
 * on the button itself, and Auto Return has to be switched on in the
 * account profile as well or PayPal keeps them on its own page. Auto
 * Return only fires once the payment actually completes, so nobody reaches
 * this page having abandoned the form partway.
 *
 * noindex, for the same reason as the newsletter thank you: a page that
 * only makes sense when you arrive from somewhere else should not turn up
 * cold in a search result.
 *
 * NO GIVE BAND. Every other page closes with an ask. Asking someone for
 * money in the same breath as thanking them for money is the one place it
 * would be wrong, so this page closes on the work instead: one band, a
 * footnote, and then the newsletter signup where every other page carries
 * the give band. Connection rather than another ask.
 *
 * The receipt language here has to keep matching Give section 05. If the
 * disclosures change, change this too.
 */
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../../../components/PageHero.astro";
import NewsletterBand from "../../../components/NewsletterBand.astro";
import { org, mailingLine } from "../../../site.config";
---

<Base
  title="Thank You"
  description="Thank you for giving to the Latimer House."
  noindex
>
  <PageHero
    crumbs={[{ label: "Thank You" }]}
    headline="Thank you. That goes into the house."
    lead="Your gift is in, and it does not sit in a fund waiting on a plan. It pays for a roof over the logs, for the brick coming off by hand, and for keeping the house and the ground around it once the work is done."
    image="/img/give-hero"
    imageAlt="The Latimer House."
    scrim={[0.94, 0.86, 0.72]}
  />
  <div class="torn-edge" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <section class="band band--parchment">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="ty">
        <div class="ty__col" data-aos="fade-up">
          <p class="eyebrow">Your receipt</p>
          <div class="stack measure ty__body">
            <p>
              PayPal has emailed you a record of the transaction already. Ours
              follows separately, because that is the one your accountant will
              want.
            </p>
            <p>
              Every gift is acknowledged in writing. A gift of two hundred fifty
              dollars or more carries the written acknowledgment the Internal
              Revenue Service requires, stating that no goods or services were
              provided in exchange for the contribution.
            </p>
            <p>
              {org.legalName}. EIN {org.ein}, a 501(c)(3) public charity.
              Contributions are deductible to the extent allowed by law.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ty__col" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="150">
          <p class="eyebrow">What happens next</p>
          <div class="stack measure ty__body">
            <p>
              The work carries on and we report it as it happens. If you would
              like to hear what came off the walls this month, there is a box at
              the foot of this page and it takes a moment.
            </p>
            <p>
              There is more to this house than the restoration. A man who was
              not family left money to save it, the house waited a long while,
              people went and read the records, and it was put right.
            </p>
            <p class="ty__actions">
              <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/the-story/">
                Read the story
                <span class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Housekeeping, and it should read as housekeeping. It was a forest
          band of its own at first, which put one dark green directly above
          the footer's dark green and read as a smudge rather than a step. */}
      <p class="foot" data-aos="fade-up">
        If something looks wrong, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${org.email}`}>{org.email}</a> and a board member will
        answer. Our mailing address is {mailingLine}. The board is unpaid and
        there is no staff, so the person who replies is the person doing the
        work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NewsletterBand
    eyebrow="One more thing"
    heading="Come along for the rest of it."
    body="You have paid for work you will not get to watch unless we tell you about it. So we will. A note when we uncover something, when we are on site, and how to join in."
    cta="Sign me up"
  />
</Base>

<style>
  .band { padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 2.25rem + 5vw, 6rem); }

  /* Two columns that become one at narrow widths, with no guessed
     breakpoint: the columns simply stop fitting and reflow. Same
     construction as the newsletter thank you, deliberately. */
  .ty {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 21rem), 1fr));
    gap: clamp(2rem, 1.25rem + 3vw, 4rem);
  }

  .ty__body { margin-block-start: 1rem; }
  .ty__body p { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  /* :not(.btn) matters. Without it this rule underlines the Read the story
     button too, because the button is an anchor inside a paragraph. */
  .ty__body p a:not(.btn) {
    color: var(--forest-900);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .ty__body p a:not(.btn):hover { color: var(--hewn-600); }

  /* The button carries its own hover transition, so the reveal animation
     goes on this wrapper instead. See the rule in global.css. */
  .ty__actions { margin-block-start: 1.75rem; }


  /* ---------- THE FOOTNOTE ----------
     A hairline and small type, ranged left under both columns. Not a band:
     it is the smallest thing on the page and should look it. */
  .foot {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 1.75rem + 3vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-block-start: clamp(1.5rem, 1.25rem + 1vw, 2rem);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted, var(--charcoal-600));
  }
  .foot a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .foot a:hover { color: var(--hewn-600); }
</style>
